      "message": "From the history of this code I found the following: we have clipContext.clip.height() \u003d\u003d 0 when the run is a placeholder with infinite font metric ascent (I assume, font size is infinite).\nThe change was introduced as a fix for one of these 2 bugs:\nPlaceholders should not be taken in MinIntrinsicWidth. \nPlaceholders should allow Inf in some style values (as weird as it sounds) \nBugs: skia:10138, skia:10159\nI have trouble reproducing the situation but I think it\u0027s still possible to come up with infinite size and non-zero width for a placeholder. That would be the case when your change will produce different (undesired) results.\nIf you ask me, infinite sizes should not be allowed in the first place.",
